From 4bd81710c46a167fb46868063a71ebe308383d51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesus Heredia <jrh06121998@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:22:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] WIP T7a (parked): twilight haze tint, stars after motion
 blur, defaults on

Parked mid-step by the PM (atmosphere deferred until after QC). Not a finished step.

In:
- Horizon band (isolated: the haze's red sky-ambient at dusk/dawn colours the fog
  floor maroon under a navy sky): voxel.Atmosphere.TwilightHaze "0.3 1 4" tints
  the haze's sky ambient through the twilight window (tint ^ TwilightSkyWeight;
  white by day and at midnight). Away side matched; sun side's step from the glow
  is 26.5 luma vs 22.6 before (known limit; "0.6 1 3" is the compromise).
- Stars: M_AtmosphereStars after motion blur plus an explicit scene-depth mask
  (that pass does not depth-test terrain). Fast-turn proof not captured yet.
- Defaults flipped in source: voxel.Atmosphere.Cycle 1, Twilight 1, Stars 1
  (Night already 1); 0 on each keeps the earlier behaviour. New test
  Unnamed.Voxel.Atmosphere.Defaults; star material pass assertion.

Reverted: moving the twilight floor after DOF (no effect on water: the engine
composites after-DOF water after that blendable).

Unverified: no Sonnet review, no RunChecks after the changes (only the d6c26416
baseline quick run), native tests not run, no hash/golden comparison with the
defaults on, /time and clock-reload checks not run. clang-format ran after the
last build (comment reflow only); rebuild before any check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
